> API and interpretation

Only ASCII nonnegative decimal strings are accepted; leading zeros and the
legacy empty-zero convention are retained. Default complete digit and actual
arithmetic/capture policies bound materialization, and every signed128
intermediate is checked. Captured products/interpolation are real recursive
producer values before carry. The old private comment mentioning-2 is corrected
to the actual+2 implementation.

Reusable producers, fixtures and histories live in the canonical C++ library.
Captured records own their values and do not come from a separate report replay.
Selected counters and record/scalar policies are specified at their API
boundaries; they are not peak-byte or wall-time budgets. Synthetic structural
inputs are controlled fixtures for these mechanisms.

